  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The first expression factors as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>. Its nonpositive set is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0222A;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>; the denominator zeros are excluded.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> The second expression is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Its strictly positive set is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0222A;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>; its numerator zeros do not satisfy the strict sign.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> The common set is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Its length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, answer D. The point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math> satisfies the first condition but not the second.</p>"
